{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Muddy Waters with the Rolling Stones feels like a natural next choice because it connects the blues and rock interests reflected in my Clapton and Hendrix listening.",
    "The acoustic blues performance appeals to my interest in rootsier music, while Old Yellow Moon and The House That Dirt Built offer plausible connections through roots-oriented songs and blues-rock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A Voice On Air 1935-1955 does not connect with the blues and rock I want right now; an older recording is not appealing simply because I enjoy established artists.",
    "I cannot connect Transitions, Stand Up, or the unspecified studio collection to my recent listening with enough confidence to choose them during an infrequent visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to stretch my interest in established musicians into a broader interest in archival recordings, which does not follow for me.",
    "A live performance or an album collection alone is not enough of a connection; I need a reason to expect music that fits my current interests."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The strongest connection is the particular blend of blues, rock, and roots-oriented music, especially when the performers make that connection clear.",
    "Something can fit my taste without being something I would choose today: soulful rock and other plausible discoveries come after the more direct blues matches."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my blues and roots-rock interests but stretched that connection too far toward archival releases and music I could not confidently connect to my listening."
}"}
